# Where the backend is. You almost certainly do NOT need to set this.
#
# Resolution order, highest first:
#
#   1. VITE_API_BASE (this file)         — an explicit override; wins everywhere.
#   2. A hosted hostname                 — anything that is not your own machine gets the committed
#                                          base in src/api/hosted.ts. This is what makes the Lovable
#                                          preview work, because Lovable does NOT inject custom
#                                          VITE_* variables into its builds.
#   3. localhost                         — relative paths through the vite dev proxy. No CORS.
#   4. nothing answers on localhost      — bundled captures (fixture mode).
#
# TO REPOINT THE HOSTED PREVIEW, edit src/api/hosted.ts — not this file. The URL is public, not a
# secret, and committing it is the only thing that survives a build that strips custom env vars.
#
# Set VITE_API_BASE only to override everything, e.g. to aim a local build at staging. A trailing
# slash and stray whitespace are tolerated. Requests then go cross-origin, so the backend must allow
# that origin, including POST with Content-Type: application/json (which preflights).
#
# For LOCAL work, retarget the PROXY instead — that is a different variable:
#   BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:9000 bun run dev --port 5273
#
# VITE_API_BASE=https://your-backend.up.railway.app
